module gunbc.systemd_directive_value_grain

import std.types { String, NonEmptyStr, Bool, List }
import std.disposition { Disposition, SingleAuthority }
import std.dissolution { DissolutionCondition, unbound_dissolution }

// WHAT THIS CARRIER IS FOR, AND WHY IT IS A FILING RATHER THAN A REPAIR.
//
// The systemd unit grammar in extdeps.systemd.unit_file models WHICH directive goes in WHICH
// section as structure -- Slice= cannot be written into [Unit], WantedBy= cannot be written into
// [Service] -- and models every directive's VALUE as a string. That is the correct boundary for a
// cited transport: systemd's own directive syntax is textual and admits several spellings per axis,
// so a grammar that refused everything but one form would be modeling a choice upstream did not
// make. The residue this module files is not that the wire is text. It is that two specific values
// arrive at that boundary having ALREADY LOST structure the tree was holding one call earlier.
//
// Filed rather than repaired because the repair is a decomposition of the directive vocabulary --
// a grammar change to a module whose byte-exact witnesses pin a live fleet timer's deployed bytes
// -- and #8827 was a renderer migration. A contract change smuggled inside a migration is read by
// reviewers who came for the migration.
//
// THE ByteSize AUTHORITY IS INTACT AND IS SPENT AT EXACTLY ONE LINE, which is the difference
// between this filing and a general complaint about stringly values. gunbc.build_cache_unit
// compile_pool_slice_unit_file receives a ByteSize and calls to_string(byte_size_count(b: sized))
// to fill SliceMemoryMax and SliceMemoryHigh. So the magnitude is modeled all the way down to the
// constructor argument and flattened there, not carried as text through the vertical -- a reviewer
// checking whether a flat scalar propagates INWARD will correctly find that it does not.
//
// WHAT IS ACTUALLY LOST is narrower and worth naming precisely: systemd.resource-control(5) accepts
// MemoryMax as a plain byte count OR with a K/M/G/T suffix OR as a percentage of installed memory,
// and the directive type cannot say which of those a given value is. Today every producer emits the
// plain count, so the loss is latent rather than live -- there is no defect to point at, which is
// exactly why it is filed rather than fixed. It becomes live the first time a producer wants a
// percentage, at which point a producer emitting a percentage and one emitting a count are
// indistinguishable to any consumer reading the directive back.
//
// STATED AS A RUNG (DESIGN section 4b): that axis sits at MITIGATABLE and its ceiling is
// structurally impossible, because membership is decidable -- the accepted forms are a closed,
// cited set. It is not a ratchet.
data systemd_directive_value_grain_scope: Disposition = SingleAuthority

// Environment { assignment: NonEmptyStr } CARRIES A KEY=VALUE PAIR AS ONE OPAQUE STRING, and the
// fusion is what makes the finding below invisible rather than being the finding itself. A
// directive type holding the variable NAME and its VALUE as two fields would make the name a thing
// the tree can be asked about; fused, the name is a substring nobody can join on.
//
// WHAT THE FUSION IS HIDING, MEASURED ON THIS TREE RATHER THAN ASSERTED. gunbc.build_cache_unit
// constructs eight Environment directives for one upstream tool's variables. THREE of them route
// through extdeps.cache.sccache functions built from modeled name rows -- sccache_start_server_env_var,
// sccache_no_daemon_env_var, sccache_idle_timeout_env_var. The other FIVE spell the upstream
// variable's name as a bare literal inside gunbc. One upstream tool's environment interface, named
// in two places by two different rules, with the split falling where it happens to have fallen
// rather than on any distinction between the variables.
//
// THAT IS THE DESIGN SECTION 3 FINDING, and it is sharper than the grammar-level one above because
// it is live rather than latent: five names of a cited dependency's interface are authored in a
// consumer. It is also the one a reader would not reach from the directive type, since the type
// shows a single NonEmptyStr and says nothing about who composed it.
//
// WHY IT IS NOT REPAIRED HERE: moving five names into extdeps.cache.sccache is an edit to the cited
// authority and belongs with the same decomposition that gives Environment its two fields -- doing
// the name move alone would leave five rows whose only consumer still concatenates them by hand,
// which is the smaller half of the fix wearing the shape of the whole.
type EnvironmentNameAuthority
  = ModeledUpstream
  | SpelledInConsumer

type BuildCacheEnvironmentVariable {
  name: NonEmptyStr
  authority: EnvironmentNameAuthority
}

// ONE ROW PER ENVIRONMENT VARIABLE THIS VERTICAL WRITES INTO THE UNIT, carrying where its NAME is
// authored. This is not a check that the names are correct -- nothing here can establish that. It
// records that one upstream tool's environment interface is named in two places by two rules, so
// the predicate below reds when that stops being true, which is the dissolution event rather than a
// regression.
//
// RUNG, DECLARED (DESIGN section 4b): MITIGATABLE. This roster is hand-authored, so a ninth
// Environment directive added to gunbc.build_cache_unit compiles clean and is simply absent here --
// the same enumeration limit gunbc.systemd_property_directive_overlap declares over its own member
// list, and for the same reason: a `.dag` source module cannot enumerate the constructor sites of a
// directive type. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER is also the same: a variant- or construction-site enumeration
// surface, at which point this list is derived and deleted rather than maintained.
data build_cache_environment_variables: List<BuildCacheEnvironmentVariable> = [
  BuildCacheEnvironmentVariable { name: "SCCACHE_START_SERVER" as NonEmptyStr, authority: ModeledUpstream },
  BuildCacheEnvironmentVariable { name: "SCCACHE_NO_DAEMON" as NonEmptyStr, authority: ModeledUpstream },
  BuildCacheEnvironmentVariable { name: "SCCACHE_IDLE_TIMEOUT" as NonEmptyStr, authority: ModeledUpstream },
  BuildCacheEnvironmentVariable { name: "SCCACHE_DIR" as NonEmptyStr, authority: ModeledUpstream },
  BuildCacheEnvironmentVariable { name: "SCCACHE_ERROR_LOG" as NonEmptyStr, authority: SpelledInConsumer },
  BuildCacheEnvironmentVariable { name: "SCCACHE_CACHE_SIZE" as NonEmptyStr, authority: ModeledUpstream },
  BuildCacheEnvironmentVariable { name: "SCCACHE_SERVER_UDS" as NonEmptyStr, authority: SpelledInConsumer },
  BuildCacheEnvironmentVariable { name: "SCCACHE_SERVER_PORT" as NonEmptyStr, authority: SpelledInConsumer },
]

// A CHECK THAT COULD NOT FAIL WAS WRITTEN HERE FIRST, AND IT IS RECORDED RATHER THAN QUIETLY
// REPLACED. The first version of this module asserted that each modeled variable name appears in
// the assignment extdeps.cache.sccache composes -- sccache_start_server_env_assignment() contains
// sccache_start_server_env_var, and its two siblings -- and called it an identity join between two
// facts one authority holds.
//
// IT IS NOT A JOIN. The composer BUILDS the assignment from the row. Both sides of the comparison
// are the same value, so the assertion is x.contains(x) and is true for every possible tree.
// Established by MUTATION rather than by rereading it: the name row was renamed to
// SCCACHE_RENAMED_BY_MUTATION and the witness still PASSED, because the rename moved both sides.
//
// THIS IS DESIGN'S OWN ORACLE RULE, in the shape it warns about -- a check that collapses to
// measure() == measure(). The correct reading of the green is not that the modeled half is verified
// but that it needs no verification: composing a value from its authority IS the construction, and
// a check restating it is the second representation section 5 says to prefer construction over. The
// five modeled variables are therefore at structurally guaranteed and have nothing to assert; the
// three unmodeled ones are the entire residue, and they cannot be asserted at all without respelling
// their literals, which would pass by construction for the same reason.
//
// So the claim is about the SPLIT rather than about either side of it: both authorities inhabited,
// in one pass over the roster.
fn environment_name_authority_is_split() -> Bool {
  (build_cache_environment_variables
     |> any(v => match v.authority { ModeledUpstream => true SpelledInConsumer => false }))
    && (build_cache_environment_variables
          |> any(v => match v.authority { ModeledUpstream => false SpelledInConsumer => true }))
}

// THE TRIGGER IS UNBOUND ON PURPOSE.
//
// The terminal shape does not delete either named declaration: SliceMemoryMax stays and its `bytes`
// field becomes a modeled value, Environment stays and its `assignment` becomes two fields. So
// neither DeclarationRetires nor DeclarationAppears fits -- the first is false because the subject
// survives, and the second would require naming a symbol nobody has declared, which is the
// fabricated-citation class. Picking a ref that makes the row LOOK bound would be that failure
// arriving by the back door, so the row states its condition in prose and is honest that no
// mechanism watches it.
data systemd_directive_value_grain_dissolution: DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(
  description: "the systemd directive vocabulary decomposes its values: SliceMemoryMax and SliceMemoryHigh take a modeled magnitude that can express the byte count, the suffixed form and the percentage form systemd.resource-control(5) admits, and Environment takes a variable name and a value as two fields rather than one fused assignment -- at which point the remaining three sccache variable names gunbc spells as literals move to extdeps.cache.sccache beside the five modeled rows. SCCACHE_DIR and SCCACHE_CACHE_SIZE moved early because the readiness producer now reads those exact upstream names as well as the renderer writing them; leaving either literal in both consumers would have grown the fork this roster exists to count. This row deletes when the value-grain work and the remaining name move land together." as NonEmptyStr,
)
